      "full_text": "scifiandfantasyreviewer July 29, 2019 Uncategorized Post navigation Previous Next Prehistoric: A Dinosaur Anthology Severed Press SJ Larsson (ed.) [Please note that a review copy was provided by one of the authors in return for a fair and honest review of this title] When I think Severed Press, I think of fast-paced, explosive action stories that usually feature some combination of dinosaurs/aliens/zombies or other terrifying creatures fighting the military, the police or perhaps a team of explorers. They\u2019re always well-written and feature intense, gun-blazing action in the best tradition of 1980s actiPrehistoric: A Dinosaur Anthology Vol. 1 \u2013 SJ Larsson (ed.) Review Introduction \"Prehistoric: A Dinosaur Anthology Vol. 1,\" edited by SJ Larsson, ventures into a realm where dinosaurs reign supreme, offering a fresh perspective distinct from Severed Press' usual fare of human vs. creature tales. This anthology transports readers to an era before humanity, where the narrative focus shifts entirely to prehistoric creatures and their world. The Editor's Vision SJ Larsson\u2019s passion for dinosaurs is evident in every meticulously crafted story within this anthology. His role as editor ensures a consistent tone that binds each tale together despite contributions from multiple authors. This consistency allows readers to immerse themselves fully, imagining the prehistoric world with vivid clarity. Standout Stories Among the contributors, Jeff Szpirer and Simon Spurrier stand out for their exceptional entries. Szpirer's story is noted for its depth and emotional resonance, while Spurrier delivers a memorable narrative that captures both action and horror elements effectively. These stories exemplify how dinosaurs can be central to compelling, multifaceted plots. Variety in Storytelling The anthology showcases a remarkable diversity of storytelling styles. From tales rich with emotional depth to those focused purely on thrilling action or unsettling horror, each story off",
